\begin{verbatim}
 TRANSFORMATION TADJPATTERN17   (*  sentential prepositional object
                                    with pro-object,
                                    without overt preposition (PARA):
                                    DUTCH: bedoeld/geschikt/MEANT 
                                 *)   

< m1: ADJPPROP{ADJPPROPrec1}
                      [mu1,
                       predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}
                              [head/ADJ{ADJrec1}[mu2],
                               argrel/SENTENCEVAR{SENTENCEVARrec1}
                              ]
                       ]
>

< m : ADJPPROP{ADJPPROPrec2}
         [mu1,
          predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}
                  [head/ADJ{ADJrec1}[mu2],
                   complrel/SENTENCEVAR{SENTENCEVARrec1}
                  ]
         ]
>

      COMP
         <
          C1: (ADJrec1.adjpatterns * [synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ,  
                                        synOPENTESENTPROOBJ
                                        ]  <> [])       AND
              (ADJPPROPrec1.adjpatternefs = []) AND
              (SENTENCEVARrec1 = { PROsubject  : true
                                   finiteness  : infinite
                                   mood        : whmod
                                   senttype    : subordinateclause
                                  }
              )

             C11: (synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
                  (SENTENCEVARrec1 = { 
                                      infsort     : omteinf
                                      }
                   )
             A11: ADJPPROPrec2 := ADJPPROPrec1;
                  ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs := [synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ]

             C12: ( synOPENTESENTPROOBJ IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
                  (SENTENCEVARrec1 = { 
                                      infsort     : teinf
                                      }
                   )
             A12: ADJPPROPrec2 := ADJPPROPrec1;
                  ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs := [synOPENTESENTPROOBJ]


          A1: @
 
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: (ADJrec1.adjpatterns * [synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ,  
                                        synOPENTESENTPROPOBJ
                                        ]  <> [])       AND
              (SENTENCEVARrec1 = { 
                                   senttype  : subordinateclause
                                   PROsubject  : true                    
                                   finiteness  : infinite
                                   mood        : whmod
                                  }
              )

              C11: (synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
                   (synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ IN ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs) 
                    AND
                   (SENTENCEVARrec1 = { 
                                        infsort     : omteinf
                                      }
                    )
              A11: @

              C12: (synOPENTESENTPROOBJ IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
                   (synOPENTESENTPROOBJ IN ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs) 
                    AND
                   (SENTENCEVARrec1 = { 
                                        infsort     : teinf
                                      }
                    )
              A12: @

          A1: ADJPrec1 := ADJPrec2;
              ADJPPROPrec1 := ADJPPROPrec2;
              ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs := [];
              ADJPPROPrec1.adjpatternefs := []  

         >


&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TADJPATTERN17
\item[* relevant examples:] 
Dit boek is niet bedoeld/(MEANT) om in te schrijven\\
Dit mes is geschikt/(MEANT) om mee te snijden\\
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) Dutch
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] AdjpPropformation
\item[* class:] TC:ADJPATTERNRULES
\item[* date of creation:] 19-SEP-1988 13:20:44  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:]
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary: Probably an abstract adjective MEANT should be added
in order to derive the cases without overt adjective. Alterntively a deletion-
transformation can be assumed.\\

\item rules: TC:CONTROL in XPPROPTOXPFORMULA should 
contain a rule that accounts for 
the identity of the PRO-object in the sentential complement and the subject.
\\
\item domain: There is special set of pattern for geschikt/bedoeld/MEANT:\\
synOPENTESENTPROOBJ, synOPENOMTESENTPROOBJ (in addition to synPREPNP and 
whatever other patterns are possible)


\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\ Dit boek is niet om in te schrijven vereist in het 
Engels een vertaling met passief: This book is not meant to be written in.\\
Soms is ook een vertaling met een for-phrase mogelijk: Dit bier is niet om op 
te drinken: This beer is not for drinking.
\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
Hier zijn twee alternatieven. Ofwel er is sprake van een extra EMPTY (of
ALL) argument; het pro-object (BIGPRO) van de te-bijzin kan dan gedeleerd
worden op basis van identitieit met EMPTY/ALL. (In dat geval verhuist de regel
naar de 2-groep.)  Ofwel het pro-object wordt gedeleerd zonder identiteit. 
Keuze is voorlopig uitgesteld. Hierboven is een variant uitgewerkt dat te 
verenigen is met het tweede alternatief.

\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}
\newpage
\begin{verbatim}

% TRANSFORMATION TADJPATTERN18a        

(* indirect object ("belanghebbend voorwerp") with preposition "para"
that should not be translated locally, while it would be incorrect 
to treat it as a prepobj. In case a paraobj can be translated 
locally it is considered a voor-obj-modifier, introduced by 
RADJVOOROBJMOD. NB. In the lexicon the adjpattern synPARANP should 
be assigned only in case the modifier treatment is not correct. *) 

< m1: ADJPPROP{ADJPPROPrec1}
                      [mu1,
                       predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}
                              [argrel/T1,
                               head/ADJ{ADJrec1}[mu2]
                              ]
                       ]
>

< m : ADJPPROP{ADJPPROPrec2}[mu1,
                       predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec2}
                              [paraobjrel/VARPREPP{VARPREPPrec1}
                                        [head/PREP(AUX_paraioprepkey){PREPrec1},
                                         objrel/T1
                                        ],
                               head/ADJ{ADJrec1}[mu2]
                              ]
                       ]
>
<

   SUBRULE (* 1 *)   
      <T1: NPVAR{NPVARrec1}>
      <T1: NPVAR{NPVARrec1}>

      COMP
         <
          C1: (synPARANP IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
              (ADJPPROPrec1.adjpatternefs = [])
          A1: ADJPPROPrec2 := ADJPPROPrec1;
              ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs := [synPARANP];
              ADJPrec2 := ADJPrec1;
              ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs := [synPARANP];
              VARPREPPrec1 := VARPREPPRECDEF;
              VARPREPPrec1.specQ := NPVARrec1.specQ;
              VARPREPPrec1.headkey := PREPrec1.key;
              VARPREPPrec1.actsubcefs:= PREPrec1.subcs;
              VARPREPPrec1.synppefs := [synNP];
              VARPREPPrec1.thetapp := pp120

         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: (synPARANP IN ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs) AND
              (synPARANP IN ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs) AND
              (synPARANP IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
              (PREPrec1.key = ADJrec1.prepkey) AND 
              (VARPREPPrec1 = VARPREPPRECDEF 
                EXCEPT FOR [synppefs, headkey, thetapp, actsubcefs, specQ]) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.specQ = NPVARrec1.specQ) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.actsubcefs = PREPrec1.subcs) AND
              (synNP IN VARPREPPrec1.synppefs) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.headkey = PREPrec1.key) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.thetapp = pp120)

          A1: ADJPrec1 := ADJPrec2;
              ADJPPROPrec1 := ADJPPROPrec2;
              ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs := [];
              ADJPPROPrec1.adjpatternefs := []  

         >

   SUBRULE (* 2 *)
      <T1: CNVAR{CNVARrec1}>
      <T1: CNVAR{CNVARrec1}>

      COMP
         <
          C1: (synPARANP IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
              (ADJPPROPrec1.adjpatternefs = [])
          A1: ADJPPROPrec2 := ADJPPROPrec1;
              ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs := [synPARANP];
              ADJPrec2 := ADJPrec1;
              ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs := [synPARANP];
              VARPREPPrec1 := VARPREPPRECDEF;
              VARPREPPrec1.specQ := yesspec;
              VARPREPPrec1.actsubcefs:= PREPrec1.subcs;
              VARPREPPrec1.headkey := PREPrec1.key;
              VARPREPPrec1.synppefs := [synNP];
              VARPREPPrec1.thetapp := pp120

         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: (synPARANP IN ADJPPROPrec2.adjpatternefs) AND
              (synPARANP IN ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs) AND
              (synPARANP IN ADJrec1.adjpatterns) AND
              (PREPrec1.key = ADJrec1.prepkey) AND 
              (VARPREPPrec1 = VARPREPPRECDEF 
                EXCEPT FOR [synppefs, headkey, thetapp, actsubcefs, specQ]) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.specQ = yesspec) AND
              (synNP IN VARPREPPrec1.synppefs) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.actsubcefs = PREPrec1.subcs) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.headkey = PREPrec1.key) AND
              (VARPREPPrec1.thetapp = pp120) 

          A1: ADJPrec1 := ADJPrec2;
              ADJPPROPrec1 := ADJPPROPrec2;
              ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs := [];
              ADJPPROPrec1.adjpatternefs := []  

         >
>
&

\end{verbatim}
